The claim contains partially accurate but highly misleading information. While Jon Bon Jovi did perform at a drive-in campaign event for Joe Biden in Pennsylvania's Luzerne County on October 24, 2020, credible sources such as the [Asbury Park Press](https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/music/2020/10/24/jon-bon-jovi-hitting-campaign-trail-big-i-vote-concert-support-biden/6022327002/) and [NBC Philadelphia](https://www.nbcphiladelphia.com/news/politics/decision-2020/bon-jovi-plays-at-biden-event-after-candidate-visits-bucks-county/2572756/) confirm the event was a drive-in rally where "hundreds of cars honked their horns," indicating a significantly larger audience than the claim suggests. The specific "12 people" figure likely refers only to non-vehicle attendees standing near the stage, while the inclusion of "7 pumpkins" is not corroborated by any source and appears to be a fabricated or distorted detail. By omitting the crucial drive-in context, the claim creates a misleading impression of a sparsely attended event, warranting a **cherry-picking** verdict.